  "body": "## What\nSingle-line freeze pin: `baseharbor-core.ref` 2adae47afddc299d06dbc34eb16a8e011c14b6dc -> **1861ed07888a1ec22c218ca491d23ee54f48e261** (immutable v0.4.26 Core anchor). Base: main at `82d042b`.\n\n## Supersedes #120\nThis PR supersedes #120 (head `bd86c7c`). #120 changed two unrelated things and drew REQUEST_CHANGES:\n- (a) the core.ref repin -> contained here, byte-identical.\n- (b) `scripts/failure-runtime-diagnostics.sh` budget changes (podman overall 60->90, per-call ceiling 20->60) -> deliberately EXCLUDED. Those are not on main and need their own qualification in a separate PR; they do not belong in a freeze pin PR.\n\n#120 is intentionally left open (superseded-by marker only).\n\n## Diff containment\n`git diff origin/main...HEAD --stat` = `baseharbor-core.ref | 2 +-` (1 file, 1 insertion, 1 deletion). No script, workflow or docs changes.\n\n## CI note (demo push-only model)\nVerified active workflow `Targeted Demo compatibility` (id 379825635) triggers only on push to `work/v0.4.2{4,5}-ecosystem-release` + `work/v0.4.26-ecosystem-release`, gated on `[demo-runtime]` message tags; no pull_request/workflow_dispatch trigger, main unprotected. So this head produces no automated checks by itself. Closest existing green run #100 (`25c3196`, both docker+podman legs) installed this same core.ref value but is not content-identical (it carries the (b) diagnostics change), so it is cited as context, not as the qualifying check for this SHA. Qualification path: maintainer-side run of the workflow over this exact candidate content (e.g. merge/cherry-pick into the release branch with `[demo-runtime]`) per repo rules; nothing dispatched from this PR.\n",
